<!-- ==========================================================
     THE THREE INDICES
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Indices</span>
      <h2>Three independent indices, not one blended guess.</h2>
      <p>Academics, athletics, and profile are scored separately &mdash; then combined.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="three-idx reveal">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M20 9 L34 15 L20 21 L6 15 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/>
            <path d="M11 18 L11 26 C11 28 15 30 20 30 C25 30 29 28 29 26 L29 18" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M34 15 L34 24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Academics</h3>
        <p>Grades and test scores, turned into the number a coach&rsquo;s preread actually runs.</p>
        <div class="gauge"><span style="width:82%"></span></div>
        <div class="gauge-cap">8.2 / 10</div>
        <span class="role">Opens the door</span>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="tag">GPA</span><span class="tag">Test scores</span><span class="tag">Course rigor</span><span class="tag">Class rank</span><span class="tag">School context</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-note">A weak input redistributes weight rather than punishing the student for it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <circle cx="26" cy="12" r="3.4" fill="#0F2A4A"/>
            <path d="M8 22 L17 18 L23 22 L30 19" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M6 28 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M6 33 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Athletics</h3>
        <p>Their times against real college swimmers &mdash; plus the direction they are trending.</p>
        <div class="gauge"><span style="width:74%"></span></div>
        <div class="gauge-cap">7.4 / 10</div>
        <span class="role">Pushes you through</span>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="tag">Competitive times</span><span class="tag">Multi-year trend</span><span class="tag">Stroke range</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-note">Versatility is measured across strokes, not event count &mdash; four freestyle times counts as one stroke.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M20 7 L23.6 15.2 L32.5 16 L25.8 21.9 L27.8 30.6 L20 26 L12.2 30.6 L14.2 21.9 L7.5 16 L16.4 15.2 Z" fill="#C9A13B" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Activities</h3>
        <p>Rated on what an activity actually took, not which category it falls into.</p>
        <div class="gauge"><span style="width:66%"></span></div>
        <div class="gauge-cap">6.6 / 10</div>
        <span class="role role-soft">Adds support</span>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="tag">Leadership</span><span class="tag">Selectivity</span><span class="tag">Impact</span><span class="tag">Initiative</span><span class="tag">Years in</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-note">Fifteen shallow clubs score lower than one four-year commitment. Titles without time behind them are discounted.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="combine reveal">
      <span class="combine-label">How they combine</span>
      <div class="equation-row">
        <span class="eq-chip">Academic Index</span>
        <span class="eq-op">+</span>
        <span class="eq-chip">Athletic Index</span>
        <span class="eq-op">=</span>
        <span class="eq-chip core">Core Score</span>
      </div>
      <div class="equation-row" style="margin-top:12px">
        <span class="eq-chip core">Core Score</span>
        <span class="eq-op">+</span>
        <span class="eq-chip adjust">Profile Index <i>(bounded adjustment)</i></span>
        <span class="eq-op">=</span>
        <span class="eq-chip final">Student-Athlete Score</span>
      </div>
      <p class="equation-caption">Profile strengthens a strong record. It can&rsquo;t sink it &mdash; and it can&rsquo;t replace it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     STANDARDIZE + BENCHMARK
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Standardize &rarr; Benchmark</span>
      <h2>Every number on the same scale. Measured against the right target.</h2>
      <p>Raw stats aren&rsquo;t comparable on their own &mdash; so we convert, then compare against each school&rsquo;s real data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-grid reveal">
      <div class="method-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="6" y="16" width="28" height="8" rx="1.5" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6"/><line x1="13" y1="16" x2="13" y2="24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="20" y1="16" x2="20" y2="24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="27" y1="16" x2="27" y2="24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Standardization</h3>
        <p>A GPA, a test score, and a swim time don&rsquo;t compare directly. Every input is converted onto one common scale before anything is combined.</p>
        <div class="method-example">3.95 GPA &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; 1480 SAT &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; 52.10 free &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; one scale</div>
      </div>
      <div class="method-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="13" y1="7" x2="13" y2="33" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M13 8 L29 13 L13 18 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <h3>University benchmark</h3>
        <p>A school&rsquo;s target isn&rsquo;t one cutoff. We rebuild that school&rsquo;s own enrolled class as a distribution from its published data, and compare against that &mdash; not a universal bar.</p>
        <div class="method-example">Public admissions data &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; most recent class &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; updated annually</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="distribution-panel reveal">
      <div class="dist-label">A school&rsquo;s enrolled-class range</div>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 600 170" width="100%" height="170" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" role="img" aria-label="A bell curve showing a school's enrolled-class range, with a sample profile plotted on the upper half">
        <defs>
          <clipPath id="rangeClip"><rect x="180" y="0" width="240" height="170"/></clipPath>
        </defs>
        <path d="M20,150 C120,150 165,18 300,18 C435,18 480,150 580,150 L20,150 Z" fill="#C9A13B" opacity="0.16" clip-path="url(#rangeClip)"/>
        <path d="M20,150 C120,150 165,18 300,18 C435,18 480,150 580,150" fill="none" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <line x1="20" y1="150" x2="580" y2="150" stroke="#DED9CC" stroke-width="1"/>
        <line x1="375" y1="150" x2="375" y2="52" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
        <circle cx="375" cy="52" r="5.5" fill="#C9A13B" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      </svg>
      <div class="dist-caps">
        <span>Less competitive</span>
        <span class="dist-legend"><i></i> Sample profile</span>
        <span>More competitive</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pull-quote reveal">A profile isn&rsquo;t good or bad. Its competitiveness depends on the university it&rsquo;s measured against.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     OUTPUT 1 — STATISTICAL COMPARISON
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Output 1 &middot; Statistical comparison</span>
      <h2>A statistical comparison, not a lookup table.</h2>
      <p>The same swimmer, checked against three different university benchmarks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ex-athlete reveal">
      <span class="ex-label">Sample athlete</span>
      <div class="ex-stats">
        <div class="ex-stat"><b>8.2</b><span>Academics</span></div>
        <div class="ex-stat"><b>7.4</b><span>Athletics</span></div>
        <div class="ex-stat"><b>6.6</b><span>Activities</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cmp-list reveal">
      <div class="cmp">
        <div class="cmp-school">Selective school</div>
        <div class="cmp-bars">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">Sample athlete</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:76%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">This school</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:66%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
        <span class="chip s">Above range</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp">
        <div class="cmp-school">Highly selective school</div>
        <div class="cmp-bars">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">Sample athlete</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:76%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">This school</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:84%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
        <span class="chip s">Within range</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp">
        <div class="cmp-school">Most selective school</div>
        <div class="cmp-bars">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">Sample athlete</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:76%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">This school</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:93%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
        <span class="chip s">Below range</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cmp-caption reveal">Nothing about the athlete changed &mdash; only the benchmark did. That&rsquo;s why the read is school-specific, not universal.</p>

    <div class="confidence-wrap reveal">
      <div class="confidence-bar">
        <div class="confidence-zone" style="left:40%;width:20%"></div>
        <div class="confidence-marker" style="left:50%"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="confidence-cap"><span>Below range</span><span>Within range</span><span>Above range</span></div>
      <p class="equation-caption">Reported as a range, not a percentage. A single number like &ldquo;87%&rdquo; hides how much the estimate could move; a range shows it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     OUTPUT 2 — THE PREREAD READ
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s navy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Output 2 &middot; Holistic Compass assessment</span>
      <h2>Grades open the door. Speed gets you through.</h2>
      <p>An academic gate and an athletic tier, read the way a selective coach&rsquo;s preread would &mdash; not a reproduction of any school&rsquo;s process.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ladder reveal">
      <div class="rung g"><span class="rung-k">Strong grades</span><span class="rung-v">In range on their own. Swimming is a bonus.</span></div>
      <div class="rung a"><span class="rung-k">Okay grades</span><span class="rung-v">Being fast helps a coach pick them.</span></div>
      <div class="rung r"><span class="rung-k">Lower grades</span><span class="rung-v">They&rsquo;d need to be a top swimmer.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="band-wrap reveal">
      <div class="band-scale"></div>
      <div class="band-caps"><span>Long shot</span><span>Fits with a push</span><span>Strong fit</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="gate-footnote reveal">Activities layers on top of this baseline. It doesn&rsquo;t replace it &mdash; and a thin activities record cannot pull a strong swimmer down more than a few points.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     LIMITATIONS
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Limitations</span>
      <h2>What the Compass does not mean.</h2>
